      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril works by blocking the angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) to lower blood pressure. Increasing the dose would likely lower it even further, not stabilize it. However, taking a higher dose may not necessarily speed up the overall effect, as it can also prolong the time it takes for the body to adjust. Your body may still experience dizziness as it adjusts to the new, lower blood pressure levels.",
